    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0512" n="1190" xml:id="pg1190"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Wood to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The President’s proclamation and news of
                    the battle at Murfreesborough reached us by the same mail. These are, I think,
                    the two greatest events of this war, and which is now begun in earnest on the
                    part of the north.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Depend upon it, that proclamation is the severest blow the confederates have
                    received this side of the Atlantic. I am glad to see that such a force has gone
                    south under Banks.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I remain, very truly, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BRADFORD R. WOOD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
